  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Isiolo Intergral Ecology Project (IIEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Isiolo Integral ecology project(IIEP) is a 3 year project currently in its 3rd year of implementation with an annual funding of &#xa3;50,000 from CAFOD General Funds effective 1st January 2023 to 31st March 2026. The project will contribute to the CAFOD  Kenya Uganda new programme strategy with the overall goal of building Resilient communities in which people, particularly women and girls, thrive in a peaceful, well-governed, and healthy, supportive natural environment.
The project  currently in 2nd year of implementation overall goal is to contribute to Strengthened environmental conservation practices and community resilience to climate related shocks in Isiolo County. This will be achieved through the following closely  interrelated outcome areas, namely;
-Target farmers, pupils and teachers adopt agro-ecological farming practices.  
-Communities implement sound environmental conservation, natural resource management and Disaster Risk Reduction interventions for improved livelihoods. 
-Secure access to community based affordable and dynamic financial services for sustainable livelihood opportunities by vulnerable households. 

This project proposes to work with three (3) schools namely Hekima, Akadeli and Kawalash and farmers in 8 areas- Leparua, Kipsing, Akadeli, Ngaresilicon, Merti, Oldonyiro, Lotulo and Ntepes. The project targets approximately 3,300 persons (594men,726women,924boys and 1056girls)</narrative>
  </description>
